{"key":"61cea1dac37472bd","source_file":"Potts Co.json","source_id":13760,"source_url":"concordance-common-sense-ppl-sensus-communis","term":"Common Sense","headwords":["Common Sense"],"latin":["Sensus communis"],"header_pairs":[{"english":["Common Sense"],"latin":["Sensus communis"]}],"header_sentences":[],"redirect_xref":null,"works":["AC","DLove","SE","TCR"],"contexts":[{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"1385","subsection":null},"text":"Hence they have less common sense...","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"2588","subsection":"end"},"text":"They are blinded to such a degree that they have no common sense, that is, they are not able to apprehend what good and truth are.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"AC","section":"3428","subsection":"end"},"text":"The simple... have a common sense of the perception of truth, but the former have extinguished that sense...","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"TCR","section":"335","subsection":"2"},"text":"They cried... He speaks against common sense...","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"TCR","section":"463","subsection":null},"text":"To deny it would be madness, because against common sense.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"SE","section":"3860","subsection":null},"text":"On the general natural sense. (See AC 4325. AC 4329.) SE 4519. SE 4521.","comment":null,"footnote":null},{"reference":{"work":"DLove","section":"8","subsection":"end"},"text":"(Common sense appealed to.)","comment":null,"footnote":null}],"slug":"common-sense","url":"/meta/potts/common-sense/"}